blames; it is also one company's water.\"}"},{"node":"n040ea2e0d0fd","v":1,"at":"1866-08-01T10:00:00+00:00","by":"farr","reason":"","body":"{\"citation\":\"CL2 (claim) in https://hypgraph.com/examples/linked/broad-street, version 1: Houses supplied by the Southwark and Vauxhall Company had 315 cholera deaths per 10,000 houses against 37 for Lambeth — 8.5 times the rate, in the same streets.\",\"hash\":\"0608c1c2d812cba1ea7f81f5256e847d8546298904d21f4e6d7d8d545b0bb75a\",\"kind\":\"primary\",\"node\":\"nfc0a914c1d64\",\"record\":\"https://hypgraph.com/examples/linked/broad-street\",\"reliability\":\"Snow's comparison of the two south London companies: the result this inquiry repeats.\",\"retrieved\":\"1866-08-01T10:00:00Z\",\"says\":\"Houses supplied by the Southwark and Vauxhall Company had 315 cholera deaths per 10,000 houses against 37 for Lambeth — 8.5 times the rate, in the same streets.\",\"url\":\"https://hypgraph.com/examples/linked/broad-street/#node=nfc0a914c1d64\",\"version\":1}"},{"node":"nffdd5faedb78","v":1,"at":"1866-08-01T10:00:00+00:00","by":"farr","reason":"","body":"{\"predictions\":[\"Deaths concentrate in the company's district, whatever the district's elevation.\",\"Neighbouring districts on other companies' water are struck far less.\"],\"statement\":\"The epidemic followed the East London Water Company's supply: the water carried it, as it did in south London in 1854.\"}"},{"node":"na12389a71134","v":1,"at":"1866-08-01T10:00:00+00:00","by":"farr","reason":"","body":"{\"predictions\":[\"Low districts suffer alike, whichever company supplies them.\"],\"statement\":\"The east end suffered because it is low-lying and crowded: the elevation law.\"}"},{"node":"nca3753ae13c6","v":1,"at":"1866-08-10T10:00:00+00:00","by":"farr","reason":"","body":"{\"aim\":\"Map the epidemic's deaths onto the water companies' districts.\",\"controls\":\"Low-lying districts supplied by other companies.\",\"method\":\"deaths by water supply, district by district\",\"proto